  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis is an old technical debt in the spec, but would probably require a lot of refactoring to get right.\r\n\r\nIn many instances, the different specs expose a function that takes a \"global object\" and then converts it to a `Document` or a different `environment settings object`. This is messy - global objects should only be used when something is specific to the JS realm, such as import maps.\r\n\r\nAs a rule of thumb, if it's not related to the global object associated things in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#realms-settings-objects-global-objects, it probably shouldn't refer to the global object.\r\n\r\nExamples for this are [queuing global tasks](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) and getting the [current time](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-relative-high-resolution-time).\r\n\r\nPerhaps as a first step we can add an informative note about this in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#realms-settings-objects-global-objects\r\n ",
